-- Written by kortopi from the data directory data, against the database shop.
-- It is the difference at the moment of the plan: 0 to insert, 1 to update, 1 to delete in 2 tables.
-- Run the statements in one transaction.

-- These settings make the values below mean what they meant to the plan. SET LOCAL keeps them until the end of the transaction.
SET LOCAL settings;

-- Tables geo.cities and geo.regions reference each other through foreign keys that are not deferrable, "cities_region" of geo.cities and "regions_capital" of geo.regions, and tables geo.cities and geo.regions have rows to write.
-- Because of the deletions, an apply with --allow-delete refuses this; one without it does not. Here the statements
-- stand in the order of the names of their tables, and once the deletions run, some of them may fail on these
-- foreign keys whatever the order. Declare one of these foreign keys DEFERRABLE.

-- geo.regions: 1 to update
UPDATE geo.regions SET 1 columns WHERE (1);

-- The deletions, in the reverse order of the foreign keys. An apply makes them only with --allow-delete,
-- so they are comments here: remove the "-- " before every line of a statement to run it.

-- geo.cities: 1 to delete
-- DELETE FROM geo.cities WHERE (10);
